{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere","id":1140145,"title":"Proposing a Death Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T06:18:07-07:00","id":1140145,"title":"Proposing a Death Sphere","content":"Many folks feel that the spheres as presented do a poor job of enabling &quot;necromancy&quot; as they envision it. if they want to raise a corpse, they need Life 2/Prime 2; if they want to travel to the Underworld, they need Entropy 4/Spirit 3/Life 2; etc. I took a stab at creating a sphere focused on these death-related things.<br /> <br /> First of all - it is mostly drawn from Spirit and focused on the Low Umbra, so if you took Spirit with that vidare you'd be halfway there. It specifically doesn't include a wide philosophical definition of &quot;death&quot; - for example, unlike in Mage: the Awakening, you can't use Death to end someone else's spell, and Death does not grant control over shadows. I wanted a Death sphere that doesn't step on every other sphere's toes, and I personally don't feel like shadow-manipulation is a key part of the &quot;necromancy&quot; I'm looking to support mechanically.<br /> <br /> Second - it is highly informed by Wraith: the Oblivion and its cosmology. This sphere would need major revision to be useful in a post-Sixth Great Maelstrom setting. That said, I've never played Wraith, so tell me where I've got it wrong.<br /> <br /> Without further ado:<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Death 1:</span></span></b></u><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Perceive across the Shroud.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Detect the weight of death on a person, object, or place - experienced, caused, or mourned by them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Death 2:</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Interact with those across the Shroud, and thicken/thin it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Place a willing wraith who is already on this side of the Shroud into an object or corpse, haunting or animating it respectively.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Call to wraiths across the Shroud, requesting their presence.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Heal own corpus if in the Shadowlands, as Life 2.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Death 3: </b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Cross the Shroud into the Shadowlands, and if one is available, follow a safe byway through the Tempest to the Dark Kingdoms.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Heal the corpus of others, as Life 3 - either while in the Low Umbra or for a manifested wraith in the Skinlands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Forge soulsteel and otherwise change its shape and purpose. Transform material objects into soulsteel by bringing them across the Shroud with you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Kill yourself by crossing into the Shadowlands without preserving the link to your body.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Maintain your life indefinitely by not allowing yourself to cross the Shroud (i.e., lichdom as long as the effect is up).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Death 4:</b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Allow others to cross into the Shadowlands or back therefrom. Create a stable gate to the Shadowlands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Forcibly place ghosts into objects or corpses, regardless of what side of the Shroud they are on.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Cause the death of others by forcing their souls across the Shroud, or deny death to those who would otherwise experience it by holding their souls on this side of the Shroud.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Death 5: </b></u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Utterly rend the Shroud, creating a Nihil - or knit one back together.</span></span><br /> - Survive travel through the Tempest. Attempt to locally manipulate the Tempest, at great peril.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Force a wraith into a Harrowing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Create Stygian steel.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">- Forge new Fetters for a wraith, or break their connection to one.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:34:43-07:00","id":1140147,"title":"","content":"As a quick response I like it. Seems well thought out as well. My only comment is the life sustaining effect at rank 3 is quite akin to a form of self possession and might be better at rank 4 for balance sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T06:16:01-07:00","id":1140500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere?p=1140147#post1140147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only comment is the life sustaining effect at rank 3 is quite akin to a form of self possession and might be better at rank 4 for balance sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah - it depends on whether you envision this sort of &quot;lichdom&quot; as simply not allowing your soul to depart after your body can no longer naturally sustain it, or if it's your ghost being placed artificially back into your remains. <br /> <br /> Obviously, if your lichdom rite only uses Death 3, you'll have a rough time - the body will continue to decay and eventually you'll just be a skeleton, and the moment someone manages to dispel the effect, you're toast. So you'd probably want to include Life 2 to &quot;reanimate&quot; your body and keep it from rotting, and some sort of Prime to either conceal or reinforce the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:25:02-07:00","id":1140545,"title":"","content":"I think becoming a Lich should be at Death 5. Also - what about the concept of a Lich's Phylactery, is it included in this Sphere Effect?<br /> Perhaps also include creating lesser Liches, like the D&amp;D's Vassaliches, with Death 5 <a href=\"http://voltor.narod.ru/vr/vr05_08.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://voltor.narod.ru/vr/vr05_08.htm</a> (described after Quasimancer) .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere?p=1140500#post1140500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the moment someone manages to dispel the effect, you're toast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Lichdom be permanent, and more or less irreversible (except perhaps through very specific Rotes or Procedures, needing a lot of successes) ? Not really something you can Unweave. A state of being rather than an Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-15-2017, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:48:35-07:00","id":1140551,"title":"","content":"Lichdom actually exists and has rules in Mage, albeit it isn't so powerful a state as D&amp;D (Aggravated damage will kill you), and can be unweaved (it still requires a lot of successes), does not need a Phylactery (albeit there's an option to have one), requires a ton of spheres (20 points, there are ways to reduce the requisites), and has a lot of downsides. It's in Dead Magic 1. I'm not sure I like those rules, albeit I do like the fact that they exist (as a sort of eastern egg).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-15-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:13:18-07:00","id":1140565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere?p=1140545#post1140545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think becoming a Lich should be at Death 5. Also - what about the concept of a Lich's Phylactery, is it included in this Sphere Effect?<br /> Perhaps also include creating lesser Liches, like the D&amp;D's Vassaliches, with Death 5 <a href=\"http://voltor.narod.ru/vr/vr05_08.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://voltor.narod.ru/vr/vr05_08.htm</a> (described after Quasimancer) .<br /> <br /> <br /> Wouldn't Lichdom be permanent, and more or less irreversible (except perhaps through very specific Rotes or Procedures, needing a lot of successes) ? Not really something you can Unweave. A state of being rather than an Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death 5 would probably make for a more practical lichdom rote, where you kill yourself, stay on this side of the Shroud, bind yourself into your remains, and forge yourself a Fetter to a phylactery. Then, people can destroy your body and disembody you that way, but as long as you are Fettered to your phylactery, you'll keep coming back and embodying yourself in other bodies. Naturally, this assumes that you would keep your Avatar and Sphere magick after your conversion into a ghost...that might require fancy amounts of Spirit or Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:36:56-07:00","id":1140572,"title":"","content":"I think that Death 5 should take care of the Avatar. Where Avatars go after death it's part of death mysteries, and Death already takes from Spirit. Life or Entropy should be used to preserve your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:16:13-07:00","id":1142716,"title":"","content":"The key issue here is that MtAs does not support any of the wizard archetypes you want. Making each sphere self-sustaining was one of the good things about nMage. In oMage if you want to be a shaman, then you need Spirit and Correspondence to summon and ward spirits, Matter to rouse to object spirits, Forces to rouse to fire/wind/light/etc. spirits, Life for animal spirits, Mind to not be fucked by all the spirits you summoned possessing you/invading your dreams, and so on, and so forth. Even the straightest archetype of &quot;I wanna kill people with fireballs real good&quot; requires Forces, Prime and then probably Correspondence.<br /> <br /> For all the good things about Mage, the way its magic system was implemented is not one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:45:08-07:00","id":1142728,"title":"","content":"This works as a minor sphere. I heavily recommend not trying to add a tenth sphere to the Ascension system. If you want Death as a full fledged sphere and lots of necromancy I recommend taking a look at mage the awakening. But in Ascension messing with ghosts is straight up spirit, with other classical necromantic effects using other spheres to accomplish similar goals. Keep in mind that the nine spheres are sort of a common, simplified &quot;language&quot; created by the traditions to break down the purviews of magic into as broad a category as they could. You want to cause a body to rot? Great a body is an inanimate object, this falls under matter. You want to bind a ghost? Cool it's an ephemeral entity, spirit has you covered. Etc. Unlike Kammerer I don't think this is a design flaw. It also has it's upsides. Wether you prefer this system or stand alone spheres is really a matter of opinion.<br /> <br /> The oft bemoaned fact that Entropy has aspects of decay coded into it is imo mostly a small impurity of the system due to the fact that the Euthanatoi hold its seat. In fact when I run the game I usually take those connotations out for non Euthanatoi and treat Entropy more as a Sphere solely based on probability, causality and similar concepts (which still enables it to break down systems of various complexity, mages loose rather little in actual ability from this distinction, except for the ability to instant rot stuff at levels 3+, still being able to render such systems unfunctional however).<br /> <br /> So tl;dr Death works well as a minor sphere for characters whose paradigm (focus, whatever M20) revolves around it, but it makes no sense as a 10th sphere as it is just a redundant mix and match of partial purviews of other spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T16:31:12-07:00","id":1142738,"title":"","content":"Agreed that you could do all these things with default Spheres and an understanding with your ST, but it would be costly in xp. I don't like when the sphere system forces you to get a dozen dots of which you'll only use a portion. Alternate Spheres - or minor Spheres - allow those character concepts. <br /> <br /> I'm not particularly enamored with the numerology of Mage: nine Spheres, nine Traditions, three Essences, three layers of the Umbra, etc. So I'd call it another Sphere like any other, but that's a pretty minor detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T01:17:10-07:00","id":1142836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere?p=1142738#post1142738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed that you could do all these things with default Spheres and an understanding with your ST, but it would be costly in xp. I don't like when the sphere system forces you to get a dozen dots of which you'll only use a portion. Alternate Spheres - or minor Spheres - allow those character concepts.<br /> <br /> I'm not particularly enamored with the numerology of Mage: nine Spheres, nine Traditions, three Essences, three layers of the Umbra, etc. So I'd call it another Sphere like any other, but that's a pretty minor detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that adding a new self-sufficient sphere doesn't solve the problem. You need to remake the whole system, not just add &quot;sphere of doing exactly what my character concept is&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T06:16:25-07:00","id":1142874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140145-proposing-a-death-sphere?p=1142836#post1142836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is that adding a new self-sufficient sphere doesn't solve the problem. You need to remake the whole system, not just add &quot;sphere of doing exactly what my character concept is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I'd do that is by borrowing the Dark Ages: Mage system and defining a Foundation and Pillars for each paradigm, but that is a hell of a lot of work. That is the path of &quot;here are four or so 'spheres' that make sense for my character&quot;, so you'd probably raise the XP costs of raising Pillars because you inherently get their full value, rather than partial value out of a sphere. <br /> <br /> I prefer that to having the luck of the draw as for how efficient the sphere dots are for your paradigm. A &quot;necromancer&quot; is screwed compared to an Etherite who concentrates on energetic physics and his pet Grand Unified Theory that allows conversion between them; the former needs like five spheres to do his stuff, while the latter can just have Forces and be done. If everyone has Pillars fitting their paradigm, they're all getting high value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T17:26:30-07:00","id":1143091,"title":"","content":"I tried to take care of this situation by generating an Alt-Sphere for Spirit that was focused on the Low Umbra. It play-tested fairly well. I just extrapolated out what Spirit as is does and then started substituting in analogues from the Low Umbra, and where the translation wasn't perfect, tried to break to down and see where it could fit. <br /> <br /> I ran Spirit as written for the mage with the Middle Umbra vidare. I didn't have to take on the High Umbra as no character was oriented that way. I did end up coming up with another Alt-Sphere version of Spirit for handling changeling issues as well.... Also worked out fairly well. <br /> <br /> It was a game with a different version of Data (which, incidentally has some definite aspects of working as Spirit for the Digital Web), a different version of Technocratic Correspondence called &quot;Space&quot; (that also worked something like Spirit a bit when used in Conventional Space in a few ways) and a Machine Sphere. And a completely retooled Entropy (which had nothing to do with Entropy, so we were working on another name... Pattern?) and Time (which got all the &quot;luck&quot; and &quot;fate&quot; aspects from Entropy)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}